# Fixer of the Fricke functions and structure of A_N

Theorem statement: `WLight.levelN_structure_package` (`61cde296-d5df-51a1-8a69-835ee824a887`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `ca744a75-f111-5c76-bb4b-4e0e37418809`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a positive natural number, and let $L$ assign to each $\tau$ in the upper half-plane
$\mathbb{H}$ a period pair with $\omega_1 = \tau$ and $\omega_2 = 1$. Let $W$ be a family of
functions indexed by $v \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ with $W_v(\tau) = (2\pi
i)^{-2}\,\wp_{L\tau}\bigl((\tilde v_0 \tau + \tilde v_1)/N\bigr)$, where $\tilde v_i$ is the
representative of $v_i$ in $[0,N)$; let $\mathrm{fricke}_v(\tau) =
-\bigl(E_4(\tau)E_6(\tau)/\Delta(\tau)\bigr)/2592 \cdot W_v(\tau)$, and let $jf(\tau) =
E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$, each pinned to these formulas by hypothesis. Put $A_N$ for the
$\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by $jf$ together with all
$\mathrm{fricke}_v$ with $v \neq 0$, and let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ act on row
vectors $v$ by $v \mapsto v\bar\gamma$, reduction mod $N$. Six assertions are made. First, the set
of $\gamma$ with $\mathrm{fricke}_{v\bar\gamma} = \mathrm{fricke}_v$ for all $v \neq 0$ is exactly
$\{\gamma : \gamma \in \Gamma(N) \text{ or } -\gamma \in \Gamma(N)\}$. Second, if $a, b \in A_N$, $b
\neq 0$, and $a \cdot (b \circ \gamma) = (a \circ \gamma) \cdot b$ for every $\gamma$, then there
are polynomials $p, q$ over $\mathbb{C}$ with $q \neq 0$ and $a \cdot q(jf) = b \cdot p(jf)$. Third,
each $\mathrm{fricke}_v$ with $v \neq 0$ satisfies a monic equation of some degree $d$ with
coefficients polynomial in $jf$. Fourth, any polynomial vanishing at $jf(\tau)$ for all $\tau$ is
zero. Fifth, every element of $A_N$ is holomorphic on $\mathbb{H}$. Sixth, $A_N$ has no zero
divisors.

This is the function-level form of the classical structure theory of the field of modular functions
of level $N$ over $\mathbb{C}$: the Fricke functions are permuted by $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$
through $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\pm\Gamma(N)$, their invariant fractions are rational in $j$, and
the algebra they generate is a holomorphic integral domain, integral over $\mathbb{C}[j]$ with $j$
transcendental. It supports the later rationality and $q$-expansion statements for forms of level
$N$, such as the description of the span of Fricke-rational products of $E_4$ and $E_6$ and the
construction of algebra homomorphisms into Laurent series.

